# 024/2: JIRA event routing by discriminator + save-time topology validation

> Part 2 of 5 in the 024-shared-board-repo-topologies plan. Parent spec: resolve `docs/specs/024-shared-board-repo-topologies.md*`.

## Summary

Wires plan 1's resolver into the JIRA router adapter so shared-key events route to the right sibling, no-match/ambiguous events are skipped with operator-readable webhook decision reasons (ambiguity additionally Sentry-captured), and the previously-silent shadowing state becomes unsaveable: the PM-integration upsert rejects a duplicate projectKey without a distinct discriminator.

Does NOT deliver read-scoping or stamping (plan 3) — after this plan, routing is correct but a shared-board project's agents still see the sibling team's items when listing. Operators should not enable sharing until plan 3 merges; this caveat is part of the plan's doc block.

**Components delivered:**
- Discriminator-aware project resolution in the JIRA router adapter (both the parse path and `resolveProject`)
- Structured skip reasons flowing into the webhook log decision reason
- Sentry capture (tag `pm_routing_ambiguous`) on ambiguity, once per issue per process
- Topology validation invoked from `upsertProjectIntegration`
- Routing-contract section in the PM integration architecture guide

**Files owned (exclusive to this plan within this spec):**
- `src/router/adapters/jira.ts`
- `src/router/platform-adapter.ts` — *(added mid-run; see Divergence below)*
- `src/router/webhook-processor.ts` — *(added mid-run; see Divergence below)*
- `src/router/config.ts` — *(added mid-run; see Divergence below)*
- `src/pm/config.ts` — *(added mid-run; type-only, see Divergence below)*
- `src/integrations/pm/_shared/topology-validation.ts` (new)
- `src/db/repositories/integrationsRepository.ts`
- `tests/unit/router/jira-project-routing.test.ts` (new)
- `tests/unit/integrations/jira-topology-validation.test.ts` (new)

**Divergence (approved 2026-08-24, mid-run):** as written this plan could not
satisfy AC #2/#3. Decision reasons on the project-resolution path are hardcoded
in `webhook-processor.ts` (`'Event unparseable or not processable'`, `` `No
project config for identifier ${…}` ``), and the adapter contract gives
`parseWebhook` / `resolveProject` no channel to supply one — both return
`T | null`. The only structured reason channel (`TriggerResult.skipReason`)
sits on the dispatch path, reachable only *after* a project resolves. Neither
file was owned by any plan in this spec.

Resolution: add an **optional** `resolveProjectWithReason` to the adapter
contract, preferred by `webhook-processor` when present and falling back to
today's `resolveProject` + hardcoded message otherwise. Being optional, the
other four adapters compile and behave unchanged — importantly `github.ts`,
which plan 4 owns, so file-disjointness with plans 3/4 is preserved. This also
corrects a message that actively misleads on shared keys: a no-match currently
reports "No project config for identifier CLFX" when config exists and simply
did not match.

`src/router/config.ts` joins the same seam for the same reason: it hand-picks
`{ projectKey, baseUrl }` into `RouterProjectConfig.jira`, so the router cannot
see `routing.discriminator` at all and could not route by it however the adapter
were written. This is the **third** appearance of that hand-pick drift class in
this spec's territory — after `configMapper.buildJiraConfig` (plan 1) and
MNG-1736's `authType`. `src/pm/config.ts`'s `JiraConfig` turned out to be a
**fourth** (typecheck caught it; the cast means data was never dropped, only the
declared type). So the JIRA config crosses four hand-written projections:

| # | Projection | Drops silently? |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `jiraConfigSchema` (Zod — source of truth) | n/a |
| 2 | `configMapper.buildJiraConfig` | yes — runtime |
| 3 | `src/router/config.ts` `RouterProjectConfig.jira` | yes — runtime |
| 4 | `src/pm/config.ts` `JiraConfig` | no — type-only cast |

Note `authType` appears in 1–3 because MNG-1736 forced it there one projection
at a time. **Worth its own follow-up ticket:** every new JIRA config field must
be added in four places, and forgetting #2 or #3 fails silently at runtime with
the field simply absent. A derived type or a round-trip conformance assertion
would make the omission a compile error instead of a production incident.

**Shared surfaces (append-only, conflicts are trivial):**
- `src/integrations/README.md` — this plan adds the "Shared-key routing contract" section; plan 3 appends a "Scoping & stamping" subsection under it

**Deferred to later plans in this spec:**
- JQL read scoping + write stamping (plan 3)
- GitHub/repo side (plan 4); wizard field (plan 5)

